# UI page patterns

When building or editing React pages:

- **Filters above content** — selectors and filters appear above tables or charts they affect.
- **Page header** — title + optional actions row; use Mantine `Title` with Title Case labels.
- **Loading / empty / error** — each list or chart handles all three states explicitly.
- **API boundary** — pages call hooks/services; no SQL or raw fetch logic duplicated across pages.
- **No chat-rationale UI** — do not add paragraphs, headers, alerts, banners, or other static text that explain what was asked for in chat or why a behavior exists. Chat instructions are for the agent; rationale belongs in `docs/`, as-built READMEs, or commit messages — not in the product UI. Show the result of the action; do not narrate it.

